+/* COURSE EDITOR CURSORS. The brush tools already draw a world-space ring on the
+   terrain — that ring IS the cursor, and it sits where the stroke will land. The
+   OS arrow on top of it was a second, differently-placed pointer competing with
+   it, so hide the arrow and let the ring do the job. Tools that place a single
+   point get a crosshair instead, because there is no ring to aim with; select
